# Intent: Two owner requests on the unit's own screens. (1) The quick settings screen had no room under the Volume and Brightness sliders, so a finger lifting from a slider could press the Wi-Fi or More button. The sliders move up (Volume row at y 50, Brightness at y 88), the saved Wi-Fi networks start at y 146 (20 px of empty space under the Brightness knob) and the bottom row (Reset, More) moves down to y 196, 6 px under the Wi-Fi row. Taps on the buttons and on the empty background are ignored for 300 ms after a slider touch ends. (2) The strip at the right of the banner row never draws the Wi-Fi glyph where the screen or the message is already about Wi-Fi: the wifi-off and bars message icons (the old rule covered wifi-off only), the connecting and Wi-Fi setup cover, and the Wi-Fi page (new maipai_banner_wifi_screen).
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc (M5Stack, patches UI01 and C02), maipai_banner.cc, maipai_banner.h (ours, N01)
# Check after a flash: Open Quick settings, drag the Volume slider and let go over the Wi-Fi row: nothing is pressed. Empty space shows under both sliders. Unplug the router: the connecting screen and the setup screen show no Wi-Fi glyph in the upper right; the face with Wi-Fi down still shows the slashed bars.
# Kconfig: none

